# Keep the shell pre-commit hook and Node enforcement scripts LF-only.
# A CRLF shell hook fails on Git Bash ("bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M") and would
# silently disable the config-drift / doc-boundary gates on a fresh Windows clone.
.githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
*.mjs               text eol=lf

# Same reasoning, different tool: nvm reads .nvmrc literally, so a CRLF byte becomes part of
# the version string and `nvm use` fails with "version '22^M' not found" on Linux/macOS - on a
# file whose whole purpose is to stop the local/CI Node skew.
.nvmrc              text eol=lf

# The vendored @smkbacil/design-ui tarball. Without this, a repo configured with
# core.autocrlf=true can line-ending-mangle the gzip stream on checkout, and the failure surfaces
# as an unreadable tarball at install time rather than as anything to do with git.
*.tgz               binary

# Dataverse solution XML is produced and consumed by Windows tooling (pac, the maker portal), so
# pin CRLF rather than letting each clone's autocrlf setting decide - a mixed-ending Solution.xml
# produces a whole-file diff on the next pac round-trip and buries the real change.
*.xml               text eol=crlf
